---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | The Little AI Company"
  description="The Little AI Company is Jeff Kazzee's one-person AI studio for useful AI tools, small apps, and learning surfaces."
>
  <section class="page-section about-page" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <header class="about-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About The Little AI Company</p>
        <h1 id="about-title">A small studio for useful AI work.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          The Little AI Company is Jeff Kazzee's one-person AI studio. It builds
          practical tools, small apps, and learning surfaces that make AI easier
          to use well.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-facts" aria-label="Studio facts">
        <div>
          <strong>Studio</strong>
          <span>One person, focused lane</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Work</strong>
          <span>Tools, apps, and learning surfaces</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Tone</strong>
          <span>Plain-spoken, warm, practical</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="belongs-title">
        <h2 id="belongs-title">What Belongs Here</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>AI tools and apps with a clear use case.</li>
          <li>Learning surfaces that help people use AI with more confidence.</li>
          <li>Project updates that show the studio getting sharper over time.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
        <h2 id="focus-title">How This Work Stays Useful</h2>
        <p>
          Each TLAC page has to make one practical job clearer: try AI, practice
          a skill, inspect a tool, or follow what is shipping.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link compact-link" href="/learn/">Find learning surfaces</a>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="selection-title">
        <h2 id="selection-title">How Projects Get Chosen</h2>
        <p>
          A project fits TLAC when it makes AI more useful, more inspectable, or
          easier to practice. The site stays small on purpose so each project has
          room to be understood.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link compact-link" href="/uses/">See the working kit</a>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section about-callout" aria-labelledby="next-title">
        <h2 id="next-title">Start With The Work</h2>
        <p>
          The clearest picture of the company is the project set: what exists,
          what is in progress, and what each project is helping sharpen.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href="/projects/">See projects</a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
